  "verbalization": "Brexpiprazole is implicated in the pathogenesis of Anxiety Disorder through its association with Major Depressive Disorder, as evidenced by multiple indirect pathways. The drug is linked to Major Depressive Disorder via its indication for this condition, and in turn, this disorder is associated with Anxiety Disorder through a chain of indications. The shared indication of Major Depressive Disorder across three distinct pathways suggests a potential role of Brexpiprazole in the pathophysiology of depression, which may contribute to the development of anxiety. The mechanisms underlying this relationship are not explicitly detailed, but the presence of a common indication for Major Depressive Disorder implies a possible overlap in biological pathways, such as neurotransmitter modulation or neuroinflammation. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Brexpiprazole may have a role in the treatment of Anxiety Disorder, though further mechanistic investigation is required to establish a direct causal link.",
